      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s incorrect. The APE header provides the actual duration of the clip and `getApeClipDurationFrames` reports it:\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:hardware/interfaces/audio/aidl/default/stub/ApeHeader.h;l\u003d57;drc\u003defc2b326cf6448ab1ff07905fec6fcd1d7164fa2\n\nSince we are not doing actual decoding, what we don\u0027t know is how much of the input compressed data (the portion of the compressed file passed at the current transfer) corresponds to how much of actual decompressed audio data. So OK, we approximate this as \"twice as much as the compressed data size\". But then, why `totalClipDurationFrames` ends up being used? If the input clip is 5 minutes long, will the `transfer` operation be stuck for 5 minutes?",
